---
import LegalLayout from "../../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const toc = [
  { id: "about",        label: "About This Policy" },
  { id: "collect",      label: "Information We Collect" },
  { id: "use",          label: "How We Use Your Information" },
  { id: "share",        label: "How We Share Information" },
  { id: "cookies",      label: "Cookies, Pixels & Tracking" },
  { id: "email",        label: "Email Communications" },
  { id: "retention",    label: "Data Retention" },
  { id: "security",     label: "Data Security" },
  { id: "children",     label: "Children's Privacy" },
  { id: "ccpa",         label: "California Rights (CCPA/CPRA)" },
  { id: "vcdpa",        label: "Virginia Rights (VCDPA)" },
  { id: "colorado",     label: "Colorado Rights (CPA)" },
  { id: "connecticut",  label: "Connecticut Rights (CTDPA)" },
  { id: "other-states", label: "Other State Privacy Rights" },
  { id: "dnt",          label: "Do Not Track" },
  { id: "international",label: "International Users" },
  { id: "changes",      label: "Changes to This Policy" },
  { id: "contact",      label: "Contact & Privacy Requests" },
];

const noticeHtml = `<p>We do not sell your personal information. This Policy explains what we collect, why we collect it, and your rights to control it.</p>`;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | GoDoDaytona"
  subtitle="How GoDoCity LLC collects, uses, shares, and protects information in connection with GoDoDaytona.com and all related services."
  pageTitle="Privacy Policy"
  effectiveDate="May 1, 2026"
  lastUpdated="May 1, 2026"
  cityBase="daytona"
  toc={toc}
  noticeHtml={noticeHtml}
>

  <!-- 1. ABOUT THIS POLICY -->
  <div class="lgSection" id="about">
    <h2>1. About This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how GoDoCity LLC ("GoDoCity," "GoDoDaytona," "we," "us," or
      "our") collects, uses, shares, and protects information in connection with GoDoDaytona.com,
      our email newsletter, social media channels, contests and sweepstakes, and all related
      services (collectively, the "Service"). By using the Service, you agree to the collection
      and use of information in accordance with this Policy.
    </p>
    <p>
      This Policy should be read together with our
      <a href="/daytona/legal/terms-of-service/">Terms of Service</a>, which govern your use of
      the Service and are incorporated herein by reference.
    </p>
    <p>
      For California residents, additional rights are described in
      <a href="#ccpa">Section 10 (California Rights — CCPA/CPRA)</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- 2. INFORMATION WE COLLECT -->
  <div class="lgSection" id="collect">
    <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>

    <h3>Information You Provide Directly</h3>
    <p>We collect information you voluntarily provide when interacting with the Service:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Newsletter subscription:</strong> email address; optionally, first name and zip code</li>
      <li><strong>Contact and advertiser inquiry forms:</strong> name, email address, business name, phone number, and the content of your message</li>
      <li><strong>Contest and sweepstakes entries:</strong> name, email address, mailing address, and any entry-specific information required by the contest rules</li>
      <li><strong>Community submissions:</strong> tips, letters to the editor, event listings, photographs, press releases, and any other content you choose to submit — including any personal information contained in that content</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Information Collected Automatically</h3>
    <p>
      When you visit the Service, we and our service providers automatically collect certain
      information about your device and browsing activity:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>IP address and approximate geolocation (typically city and state level)</li>
      <li>Browser type, version, and language settings</li>
      <li>Operating system and device type (desktop, mobile, tablet)</li>
      <li>Pages visited, links clicked, scroll depth, and time spent on page</li>
      <li>Referring URL (the page or platform you came from before visiting our Service)</li>
      <li>UTM parameters and campaign tracking codes in URLs</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This information is collected through cookies, pixels, and similar tracking technologies
      as described in <a href="#cookies">Section 5</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>Information from Third Parties</h3>
    <p>We may receive information about you from the following third-party sources:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Social media platforms</strong> when you interact with our social media accounts, share our content, or connect with us through a social platform</li>
      <li><strong>Advertising and analytics partners</strong> who provide aggregated and anonymized data for advertising performance measurement — this does not include your name or email address</li>
      <li><strong>Contest co-sponsors</strong> who may share information you provided during a jointly administered contest or sweepstakes for purposes of prize fulfillment</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <!-- 3. HOW WE USE YOUR INFORMATION -->
  <div class="lgSection" id="use">
    <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <p>We use the information we collect for the following purposes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Deliver our newsletter and editorial content to subscribers</li>
      <li>Respond to inquiries, advertiser requests, and community submissions</li>
      <li>Improve the Service through analytics, user research, and testing</li>
      <li>Administer contests, sweepstakes, and community programs</li>
      <li>Send transactional emails related to your specific requests or account activity</li>
      <li>Detect and prevent fraud, abuse, spam, and technical issues</li>
      <li>Comply with applicable legal obligations and enforce our Terms of Service</li>
      <li>Measure and analyze the effectiveness of advertising (aggregated; never sold)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Where required by applicable law, our legal bases for processing personal data include:
      <strong>performance of a contract</strong> (e.g., delivering newsletter content you
      subscribed to); <strong>legitimate interests</strong> (e.g., improving the Service,
      preventing fraud and abuse, operating our business); <strong>consent</strong> (where
      explicitly obtained from you, such as for certain cookies or communications); and
      <strong>legal compliance</strong> (processing required by applicable law).
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- 4. HOW WE SHARE INFORMATION -->
  <div class="lgSection" id="share">
    <h2>4. How We Share Information</h2>

    <h3>Service Providers</h3>
    <p>
      We share data with third-party vendors who act as data processors on our behalf. These
      include email delivery and newsletter platforms (such as Mailchimp or similar services),
      web hosting and content delivery network (CDN) providers, web analytics tools (such as
      Google Analytics), contest and sweepstakes administration platforms, and payment
      processors for advertising sales. All such vendors process your data solely under our
      instructions, pursuant to written data processing agreements, and are prohibited from
      using your personal data for their own independent purposes.
    </p>

    <h3>Advertising</h3>
    <p>
      We work with third-party advertising networks and analytics providers who may collect
      information through cookies, pixels, and similar tracking technologies placed on our
      pages. This data is used to measure advertising performance and may be used by these
      networks to serve interest-based or targeted advertising on other platforms. Please see
      <a href="#cookies">Section 5 (Cookies, Pixels &amp; Tracking)</a> for more information
      and opt-out options.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>We do not share your name, email address, or other directly identifying
      personal information with advertisers.</strong>
    </p>

    <h3>Legal &amp; Safety Disclosures</h3>
    <p>
      We may disclose your information to law enforcement, government authorities, or other
      third parties when: (a) required by applicable law, regulation, subpoena, or court order;
      (b) we believe in good faith that disclosure is necessary to protect the rights, property,
      or safety of GoDoCity LLC, our users, or the general public; or (c) we are investigating
      suspected fraud, violations of our Terms of Service, or other unlawful activity.
    </p>

    <h3>Business Transfers</h3>
    <p>
      In the event of a merger, acquisition, reorganization, bankruptcy, or sale of all or
      substantially all of GoDoCity LLC's assets, user information may be transferred as part
      of that transaction. We will provide notice to you — by updating this Privacy Policy
      and, where practicable, by emailing newsletter subscribers — before any such transfer
      occurs, and we will describe the options available to you at that time.
    </p>

    <h3>Aggregated and De-Identified Data</h3>
    <p>
      We may share aggregated, de-identified, or anonymized information — such as
      "approximately 35% of our readers are between the ages of 25 and 44" — with partners,
      advertisers, and the public. Such information cannot reasonably be used to identify you
      individually and is not subject to this Privacy Policy.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- 5. COOKIES, PIXELS & TRACKING -->
  <div class="lgSection" id="cookies">
    <h2>5. Cookies, Pixels &amp; Tracking</h2>

    <h3>What We Use</h3>
    <p>
      We and our third-party partners use cookies, web beacons, pixels, local storage objects,
      and similar tracking technologies (collectively, "Tracking Technologies") to operate,
      maintain, and improve the Service, and to deliver and measure advertising.
    </p>

    <h3>Types of Tracking Technologies</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Session Cookies:</strong> Temporary cookies stored in your browser's memory that expire automatically when you close your browser session. Used to maintain session state and enable core Service functionality during your visit.</li>
      <li><strong>Persistent Cookies:</strong> Cookies stored on your device for a defined period of time, even after you close your browser. Used to remember your preferences and recognize you as a returning visitor.</li>
      <li><strong>Web Beacons / Pixels:</strong> Small transparent image files (1x1 pixels) or short snippets of code embedded in web pages and emails. When loaded, they send a signal to a server confirming that a page has been viewed or an email has been opened. Used to measure content and email engagement.</li>
      <li><strong>Third-Party Pixels:</strong> Code placed on our pages by third-party platforms to enable advertising measurement, remarketing, and analytics functionality (described in detail below).</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Specific Technologies We Use</h3>

    <h4>Google Analytics</h4>
    <p>
      We use Google Analytics to understand how visitors interact with the Service, including
      which pages are visited, session duration, traffic sources, and user demographics
      (aggregated). Google Analytics sets cookies to collect this behavioral data, which is
      transmitted to and stored by Google on servers in the United States and other countries.
      We have enabled IP anonymization to truncate IP addresses before storage. You may opt
      out of Google Analytics data collection by installing the
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
    </p>

    <h4>Google Tag Manager</h4>
    <p>
      We use Google Tag Manager ("GTM") to deploy and manage analytics tags, tracking scripts,
      and other code snippets on the Service without requiring direct code changes. GTM itself
      does not collect personal data, but it may load other tracking scripts as described in
      this Section.
    </p>

    <h4>Meta (Facebook) Pixel</h4>
    <p>
      We use the Meta Pixel (formerly Facebook Pixel) to measure the effectiveness of
      advertising we run on Facebook and Instagram, and to enable remarketing to users who
      have previously visited the Service. When you visit certain pages of our Service, the
      Meta Pixel transmits certain behavioral data to Meta Platforms, Inc. You may opt out
      of interest-based advertising through
      <a href="https://www.facebook.com/settings?tab=ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Facebook's ad settings</a>
      or through the opt-out tools listed below.
    </p>

    <h4>Email Tracking Pixels</h4>
    <p>
      Our newsletter emails contain a single transparent pixel image that confirms when an
      email has been opened and whether embedded links have been clicked. This data is used
      solely to measure newsletter engagement and improve content quality. To prevent email
      open tracking, you may disable automatic image loading in your email client settings.
    </p>

    <h4>Newsletter Service Provider Tracking</h4>
    <p>
      Our email delivery platform sets cookies on our website and tracks user engagement with
      our newsletter (including opens, clicks, and unsubscribes) in accordance with its own
      privacy policy and data processing agreement with GoDoCity LLC.
    </p>

    <h3>Cookie Controls</h3>
    <p>You have several options for controlling tracking technologies:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Browser settings:</strong> Most modern web browsers allow you to block, delete, or be notified about cookies through your browser's privacy or security settings. Please consult your browser's help documentation for instructions.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Analytics opt-out:</strong> Install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a> to prevent your data from being used by Google Analytics across all websites.</li>
      <li><strong>Industry opt-out tools:</strong> Opt out of interest-based advertising from participating companies via the <a href="http://optout.networkadvertising.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Network Advertising Initiative (NAI) opt-out tool</a> or the <a href="http://optout.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Digital Advertising Alliance (DAA) opt-out tool</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Cookie consent:</strong> Where required by applicable law (such as for users in the EU/UK), we will obtain your consent before placing non-essential cookies.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Please note that blocking or deleting certain cookies may affect the functionality of
      some features of the Service. Opting out of interest-based advertising does not mean
      you will see fewer ads — only that ads may be less relevant to your interests.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- 6. EMAIL COMMUNICATIONS -->
  <div class="lgSection" id="email">
    <h2>6. Email Communications</h2>
    <p>
      Newsletter subscribers receive regular emails containing local news, events, dining
      guides, business spotlights, community announcements, and advertising. You may
      unsubscribe from newsletter emails at any time by clicking the unsubscribe link
      included in every marketing email, or by emailing us at
      <a href="mailto:hello@gododaytona.com">hello@gododaytona.com</a> with "unsubscribe"
      in the subject line. We process unsubscribe requests within ten (10) business days.
    </p>
    <p>
      Transactional emails — including contest entry confirmations, inquiry responses, and
      account-related notices — are sent as needed in connection with your specific requests
      and are not subject to marketing unsubscribe requirements.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>We do not sell, rent, or share your email address with third parties for
      their own marketing or promotional purposes.</strong>
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- 7. DATA RETENTION -->
  <div class="lgSection" id="retention">
    <h2>7. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>
      We retain personal information only for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes for
      which it was collected and to comply with our legal obligations. Our general retention
      practices are as follows:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Newsletter subscribers:</strong> Email address and subscription data are retained while your subscription is active. After you unsubscribe, your email address is retained in a suppression list to prevent inadvertent re-enrollment.</li>
      <li><strong>Contact form submissions:</strong> Retained for up to twenty-four (24) months from the date of submission.</li>
      <li><strong>Contest entry data:</strong> Retained for the duration required to administer the contest, fulfill legal and prize obligations, and satisfy any applicable statutory record-keeping requirements, then deleted or anonymized.</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics data:</strong> Retained in accordance with Google Analytics default retention settings (26 months by default, which we may adjust based on our needs and applicable law).</li>
      <li><strong>Security and access logs:</strong> Retained for up to twelve (12) months.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We may retain certain information for longer periods where required by law, to resolve
      disputes, enforce our agreements, or for legitimate business purposes such as fraud
      prevention.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- 8. DATA SECURITY -->
  <div class="lgSection" id="security">
    <h2>8. Data Security</h2>
    <p>
      We implement technical and organizational security measures designed to protect your
      personal information from unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration, or destruction.
      These measures include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>HTTPS/TLS encryption for all data transmitted between your browser and the Service</li>
      <li>Access controls limiting who within our organization can access personal data, based on need</li>
      <li>Vendor agreements requiring service providers to maintain appropriate technical and organizational security measures</li>
      <li>Regular review of our data collection, storage, and processing practices</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      No method of electronic transmission or data storage is completely secure. While we
      strive to use commercially acceptable means to protect your personal information, we
      cannot guarantee absolute security. In the event of a data breach that materially
      affects your personal information, we will notify you as required by applicable law.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- 9. CHILDREN'S PRIVACY -->
  <div class="lgSection" id="children">
    <h2>9. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is not directed to, and is not intended for use by, children under the age
      of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you
      are a parent or guardian and believe that your child under 13 has provided personal
      information to us through the Service, please contact us immediately at
      <a href="mailto:hello@gododaytona.com">hello@gododaytona.com</a> and we will take
      prompt steps to delete that information from our records.
    </p>
    <p>
      For users in the European Union or United Kingdom, the minimum age for consent to
      data processing is 16 years (or such lower age as may be permitted under the laws of
      the user's Member State or country), except where verifiable parental consent has been
      obtained in accordance with applicable law.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- 10. CALIFORNIA RIGHTS (CCPA / CPRA) -->
  <div class="lgSection" id="ccpa">
    <h2>10. California Rights (CCPA/CPRA)</h2>

    <h3>Your California Privacy Rights</h3>
    <p>
      If you are a California resident, the California Consumer Privacy Act of 2018 (CCPA),
      as amended and expanded by the California Privacy Rights Act of 2020 (CPRA),
      grants you specific rights regarding your personal information. This section describes
      those rights and how to exercise them.
    </p>

    <h4>Right to Know</h4>
    <p>
      You have the right to request that we disclose: (a) the categories of personal
      information we have collected about you; (b) the specific pieces of personal information
      we have collected about you; (c) the categories of sources from which we collected the
      information; (d) the business or commercial purpose for collecting, sharing, or selling
      the information; and (e) the categories of third parties with whom we share the information.
    </p>

    <h4>Right to Delete</h4>
    <p>
      You have the right to request that we delete personal information we have collected
      from you, subject to certain exceptions. We may deny a deletion request where retaining
      the information is necessary to: complete a transaction, detect security incidents,
      debug errors, comply with a legal obligation, engage in research in the public interest,
      or enable internal uses reasonably aligned with your expectations.
    </p>

    <h4>Right to Correct</h4>
    <p>
      You have the right to request correction of inaccurate personal information we maintain
      about you, taking into account the nature of the information and our purposes for
      processing it.
    </p>

    <h4>Right to Opt Out of Sale / Sharing</h4>
    <p>
      <strong>We do not sell personal information.</strong> We do not share personal
      information for cross-context behavioral advertising as defined by the CPRA.
      No opt-out action is required with respect to sale or sharing of personal information.
    </p>

    <h4>Right to Limit Use of Sensitive Personal Information</h4>
    <p>
      We do not collect or use sensitive personal information (as defined by the CPRA, such
      as Social Security numbers, precise geolocation, racial or ethnic origin, health data,
      or biometric data) beyond what is strictly necessary to provide the Service to you.
    </p>

    <h4>Right to Non-Discrimination</h4>
    <p>
      We will not discriminate against you for exercising any of your CCPA/CPRA rights.
      We will not deny you goods or services, charge you different prices, provide a
      different level of service quality, or suggest that you will receive different
      treatment for exercising your rights.
    </p>

    <h4>Categories of Personal Information Collected</h4>
    <p>
      In the preceding twelve (12) months, we have collected the following categories of
      personal information (per CCPA statutory categories):
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Identifiers:</strong> Email address, IP address, and cookie identifiers</li>
      <li><strong>Internet or other electronic network activity information:</strong> Pages visited, links clicked, scroll behavior, session duration, and traffic source</li>
      <li><strong>Geolocation data:</strong> City- and state-level approximation derived from IP address</li>
      <li><strong>Commercial information:</strong> Advertising purchase records (applicable to advertisers only)</li>
      <li><strong>Inferences:</strong> Inferences drawn from the above categories to create a profile about a user's preferences and interests, used for internal analytics purposes</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>Categories of Third Parties with Whom Information Is Shared</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Service providers (analytics platforms, email delivery services, web hosting)</li>
      <li>Advertising measurement partners (aggregated/anonymized performance data only)</li>
      <li>Legal authorities and law enforcement (when required by law)</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>How to Exercise Your California Rights</h4>
    <p>
      To submit a request to know, delete, or correct, please email
      <a href="mailto:hello@gododaytona.com">hello@gododaytona.com</a> with the subject
      line <strong>"California Privacy Request."</strong> We will verify your identity before
      processing your request to prevent unauthorized disclosure. We will respond to
      verifiable requests within forty-five (45) calendar days of receipt. If we require
      additional time, we will notify you and may extend our response period by an additional
      forty-five (45) days.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may designate an authorized agent to make a CCPA request on your behalf. Authorized
      agents must provide written proof of authorization, and we may require you to directly
      verify your identity with us before processing the request.
    </p>

    <h4>Shine the Light</h4>
    <p>
      California Civil Code § 1798.83 ("Shine the Light" law) permits California residents
      to request information about personal information we have shared with third parties
      for their direct marketing purposes in the preceding calendar year. <strong>We do not
      share personal information with third parties for their own direct marketing
      purposes.</strong> Accordingly, no such disclosure is applicable.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- 11. VIRGINIA RIGHTS (VCDPA) -->
  <div class="lgSection" id="vcdpa">
    <h2>11. Virginia Rights (VCDPA)</h2>
    <p>
      If you are a Virginia resident, the Virginia Consumer Data Protection Act (VCDPA)
      grants you the following rights with respect to your personal data:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>The right to confirm whether we are processing your personal data</li>
      <li>The right to access the personal data we have collected about you</li>
      <li>The right to correct inaccuracies in your personal data</li>
      <li>The right to delete personal data you have provided to us or that we have collected about you</li>
      <li>The right to obtain a portable copy of personal data you have provided to us, in a format that is readily usable</li>
      <li>The right to opt out of: (a) targeted advertising; (b) the sale of personal data; and (c) profiling in furtherance of decisions that produce legal or similarly significant effects concerning you</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>We do not sell personal data</strong> and <strong>do not engage in profiling</strong> that produces legal effects or similarly significant effects.
    </p>
    <p>
      To exercise your Virginia privacy rights, please email
      <a href="mailto:hello@gododaytona.com">hello@gododaytona.com</a> with the subject
      line <strong>"Virginia Privacy Request."</strong> We will respond within forty-five
      (45) days of receipt; we may extend our response period by an additional forty-five
      (45) days when reasonably necessary, with prior notice. If we decline to act on your
      request, you may appeal our decision by emailing
      <a href="mailto:legal@godocity.com">legal@godocity.com</a> with the subject line
      "Virginia Privacy Appeal," and we will respond within sixty (60) days.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- 12. COLORADO RIGHTS (CPA) -->
  <div class="lgSection" id="colorado">
    <h2>12. Colorado Rights (CPA)</h2>
    <p>
      If you are a Colorado resident, the Colorado Privacy Act (CPA) grants you the following
      rights with respect to your personal data:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>The right to access personal data we have collected about you</li>
      <li>The right to correct inaccuracies in your personal data</li>
      <li>The right to delete personal data concerning you</li>
      <li>The right to obtain a portable copy of personal data you have provided to us</li>
      <li>The right to opt out of targeted advertising, sale of personal data, and profiling in furtherance of decisions with legal or significant effects</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>We do not sell personal data.</strong> To exercise your Colorado privacy rights,
      please email <a href="mailto:hello@gododaytona.com">hello@gododaytona.com</a> with the
      subject line <strong>"Colorado Privacy Request."</strong> We will respond within
      forty-five (45) days of receipt, with the option to extend by an additional forty-five
      (45) days upon notice. You may appeal a denial by emailing
      <a href="mailto:legal@godocity.com">legal@godocity.com</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- 13. CONNECTICUT RIGHTS (CTDPA) -->
  <div class="lgSection" id="connecticut">
    <h2>13. Connecticut Rights (CTDPA)</h2>
    <p>
      If you are a Connecticut resident, the Connecticut Data Privacy Act (CTDPA) grants you
      the following rights with respect to your personal data:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>The right to access personal data we process about you</li>
      <li>The right to correct inaccuracies in your personal data</li>
      <li>The right to delete personal data concerning you</li>
      <li>The right to obtain a portable copy of personal data you have provided to us</li>
      <li>The right to opt out of targeted advertising, sale of personal data, and profiling in furtherance of solely automated decisions with legal or similarly significant effects</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>We do not sell personal data.</strong> To exercise your Connecticut privacy
      rights, please email <a href="mailto:hello@gododaytona.com">hello@gododaytona.com</a>
      with the subject line <strong>"Connecticut Privacy Request."</strong> We will respond
      within forty-five (45) days; we may extend our response by an additional forty-five (45)
      days with notice. You may appeal a decision by emailing
      <a href="mailto:legal@godocity.com">legal@godocity.com</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- 14. OTHER STATE PRIVACY RIGHTS -->
  <div class="lgSection" id="other-states">
    <h2>14. Other State Privacy Rights</h2>
    <p>
      We recognize that additional state privacy laws have been enacted or are taking effect
      across the United States. These include, but are not limited to, laws in Nevada, Utah,
      Iowa, Indiana, Tennessee, Montana, Oregon, Texas, Delaware, New Hampshire, New Jersey,
      and other states. Where applicable and to the extent required by law, we will honor
      rights granted to residents under these statutes.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you believe you have privacy rights under your state's applicable law that are not
      addressed in this Privacy Policy, or if you would like to understand how this Policy
